Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tcpm: ask a powered partner for the sink role

A charge-through dock whose own supply goes away for a moment falls back
to an unpowered sink.  A port that prefers the sink role finds no Rp in
Try.SNK and becomes the dock's power source.  One hub (291a:8383) then
said nothing at all for 26 minutes, also when its charger was pulled and
plugged in again: no PD message and no CC change, while the port powered
it and its USB devices from a tablet battery, until the hub was
re-plugged.  The same hub accepts a PR_Swap from the port once its supply
is back.

Let the TCPC opt in to asking.  With tcpc->request_sink_as_source set, a
port that is Source to a PD partner under an explicit contract, and that
prefers the sink role, sends Get_Source_Cap (new states GET_SOURCE_CAP
and GET_SOURCE_CAP_TIMEOUT, in the AMS GET_SOURCE_CAPABILITIES) and
requests a PR_Swap when the vSafe5V PDO of the answer has Unconstrained
Power.  That answer is the only one that ever leads to a PR_Swap.  The
swap is TCPM's own PR_Swap, requested as tcpm_pr_set() does with nobody
waiting; its success and failure paths are unchanged.

The first question goes out 5 s after the first SRC_READY with an
explicit contract.  A partner without external power is asked again
after 30 s, then 60, 120, 240 and 480 s, then every 10 minutes, since its
supply can come back at any time.  Reject or Not_Supported to
Get_Source_Cap, or no answer to it, is asked again every 10 minutes: a
charge-through dock may well be a plain sink while its supply is away.
Wait to either message is asked again one step further down the ladder,
and so are Reject and no answer to the PR_Swap, bounded by the requests
per session below.  Reject to the PR_Swap from a partner whose PDO does
not claim dual-role power, Not_Supported to it, and capabilities that do
not start with a fixed supply stop the questions for the session.  The
Dual-Role Power bit alone does not decide: the hub above passes its
charger's flags on, announced no dual-role power with one of its
chargers, and accepted the PR_Swap all the same.

The questions belong to a session: one partner while it stays attached,
or comes back within a minute of a port reset, as the partner of a
failed swap does.  The port cannot tell partners apart across a reset,
so another partner plugged in within that minute continues the session.
A question or a PR_Swap that is on the wire when a port reset, a Soft
Reset or a Hard Reset comes, or that was sent less than 2 s before a
port reset and not answered, stops the session: a partner that leaves
the bus on either gets it once per session, and the reset counts as a
failed swap if the partner then stays away for longer than the minute.
One that was queued and never sent is asked again later.

An accepted swap is settled at the next ready state, also when an error
recovery comes in between: SNK_READY with a contract is the swap done,
SRC_READY means the partner took it and could not supply power.  That,
and a sink role lost within a minute of the swap with the port source
again in the same session (a supply that collapses under the port's
load; an unplug is not one), is a failed swap and stops the session.  An
accepted swap still unsettled when its partner has been gone for longer
than the minute counts as failed as well.  Per session at most eight
requests and three accepted swaps are made; a sink role from a swap that
lasted 10 minutes gives both back, so that a supply that drops now and
then is followed each time.  After two failed swaps nothing is asked in
any session until a sink stint of 30 minutes has ended.  A partner used
without its supply on purpose, or one that leaves the bus on a question,
therefore sees at most one reconnect per session (in practice per
plug-in), two in all while it keeps taking longer than a minute to come
back, none from then on until such a sink stint, and never a loop.

Others' choices stand.  A write of "source" to power_role stops the
session and drops a request that has not gone out yet; a write of "sink"
takes over one that is queued or due.  A PR_Swap that the partner asks
for and that makes the port source stops the session as well, and a
queued question is dropped when the partner's PR_Swap is accepted, since
it would go out in the other power role.  A write of preferred_role that
makes the port prefer the sink role again resumes the questions.

The work starts nothing while the VDM state machine runs, discovery is
due, an AMS is open or a state change is queued, and GET_SOURCE_CAP sends
nothing unless the AMS is still the question's: a write or a partner
message that comes in during the tSinkTx wait goes first, and the
question is asked again a second later.  While the port stays busy that
is every second for a minute, then one step down the ladder.  The work
is deferrable and runs on a freezable workqueue: it never wakes an idle
CPU and does nothing while the system sleeps.  Each request, each answer
to it, the first "no external power" and the first "not a source now"
answer to Get_Source_Cap in a session, and each reason to stop is one
dev_info() line, formatted once for both the kernel log and the TCPM
log; the other answers go to the TCPM log only.

Upstream sets the AMS GET_SOURCE_CAPABILITIES when the partner asks for
the port's own source capabilities, and takes Source_Capabilities in it
as Source, but the port never asked for the partner's as Source.  That
handling is completed for the new state: the answer in GET_SOURCE_CAP
goes back to SRC_READY with the AMS still set, so that tcpm_ams_finish()
gives the sink SinkTxOK back, and Reject, Wait or Not_Supported that come
in GET_SOURCE_CAP no longer end in a Soft Reset.  Answers that come after
the 60 ms timeout take upstream's path unchanged: a late Reject, Wait or
Not_Supported a Soft Reset, late Source_Capabilities a Not_Supported (a
Reject below PD 3.0).  Both new states are source states for a CC or
VBUS change.

Ports whose TCPC does not set the flag are not affected.  Written,
compiled and run in a host harness of the bookkeeping; not run on
hardware.
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c |  868 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/usb/tcpm.h      |   12 +
 2 files changed, 877 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpm.c
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 #include <linux/usb/role.h>
 #include <linux/usb/tcpm.h>
 #include <linux/usb/typec_altmode.h>
+#include <linux/workqueue.h>
 
 #include <uapi/linux/sched/types.h>
 
@@ -145,6 +146,8 @@
 						\
 	S(GET_SINK_CAP),			\
 	S(GET_SINK_CAP_TIMEOUT),		\
+	S(GET_SOURCE_CAP),			\
+	S(GET_SOURCE_CAP_TIMEOUT),		\
 						\
 	S(ERROR_RECOVERY),			\
 	S(PORT_RESET),				\
@@ -280,6 +283,27 @@ enum frs_typec_current {
 #define SINK_DFP_SWAP_TRIES	3
 #define SINK_DFP_SWAP_WAIT_MS	100
 
+/*
+ * tcpc->request_sink_as_source, the swap back to sink (see
+ * tcpm_swap_back_work()): when the first question goes out, the ladder of
+ * waits after an answer that is not "yes", the retry while the port is busy
+ * and how long it lasts, how long after a question a reset counts against
+ * it, and the bounds.
+ */
+#define SWAP_BACK_FIRST_MS		5000U
+#define SWAP_BACK_POLL_MIN_MS		30000U
+#define SWAP_BACK_POLL_MAX_MS		600000U
+#define SWAP_BACK_RETRY_MS		1000U
+#define SWAP_BACK_BUSY_MAX_MS		60000U
+#define SWAP_BACK_CUT_MS		2000U
+#define SWAP_BACK_MAX_REQUESTS		8U
+#define SWAP_BACK_MAX_ACCEPTED		3U
+#define SWAP_BACK_MAX_STRIKES		2U
+#define SWAP_BACK_SESSION_GAP_MS	60000U
+#define SWAP_BACK_SINK_SHORT_MS		60000U
+#define SWAP_BACK_SINK_REFUND_MS	(10U * 60 * 1000)
+#define SWAP_BACK_SINK_STABLE_MS	(30U * 60 * 1000)
+
 struct pd_mode_data {
 	int svid_index;		/* current SVID index		*/
 	int nsvids;
@@ -431,6 +455,76 @@ enum aug_req_type {
 	PD_SPR_AVS,
 };
 
+/*
+ * struct swap_back_data - tcpc->request_sink_as_source, the swap back to sink
+ * @work: the next question or request; deferrable, on a freezable workqueue
+ *
+ * One session per partner: it goes on while the partner stays attached and
+ * across a reconnect, and ends when the port has been without a partner for
+ * SWAP_BACK_SESSION_GAP_MS (see tcpm_swap_back_ready()).
+ * @reset_at: last port reset (boot time, so that a system sleep counts)
+ * @requests: PR_Swap requests made in this session
+ * @accepted: of these, the ones the partner accepted
+ * @stopped: no more questions in this session
+ * @told_no_power: "no external power" is in the kernel log for this session
+ * @told_refused: "not a source now" is in the kernel log for this session
+ *
+ * Until a sink stint of SWAP_BACK_SINK_STABLE_MS has ended:
+ * @strikes: failed swaps
+ *
+ * Until the next ready state, across a port reset:
+ * @pending: a PR_Swap of the swap back's was accepted, outcome not known yet
+ * @pending_reset: the port was reset while @pending
+ * @unsettled: a question or request was cut short by a port reset
+ * @lost_early: the sink role of a swap ended within SWAP_BACK_SINK_SHORT_MS
+ *
+ * Per attach (cleared by tcpm_swap_back_reset()):
+ * @armed: scheduled since the first SRC_READY with an explicit contract
+ * @seen_ready: a ready state has been reached since the reset
+ * @probing: a Get_Source_Cap of the swap back's is queued or under way
+ * @probe_sent: it went out, and neither an answer nor the timeout came yet
+ * @pr_due: the partner's capabilities said yes; request the swap next
+ * @pr_queued: the swap back's PR_Swap waits in upcoming_state
+ * @pr_sent: the PR_Swap in PR_SWAP_SEND is the swap back's, not answered yet
+ * @sent_pr: what went out last was a PR_Swap (else a Get_Source_Cap)
+ * @partner_drp: the partner's vSafe5V PDO claims dual-role power
+ * @interval_ms: the next wait on the ladder after an answer that is not "yes"
+ * @due: jiffies at which @work is meant to run
+ * @busy_since: the port has been busy since (boot time; 0 when not)
+ * @sent_at: when the last question or request went out, until answered
+ * @sink_at: start of the current sink stint (boot time; 0 when source)
+ * @sink_by_swap: that sink stint came from a swap of the swap back's
+ */
+struct swap_back_data {
+	struct delayed_work work;
+	ktime_t reset_at;
+	unsigned int requests;
+	unsigned int accepted;
+	bool stopped;
+	bool told_no_power;
+	bool told_refused;
+	unsigned int strikes;
+	bool pending;
+	bool pending_reset;
+	bool unsettled;
+	bool lost_early;
+	bool armed;
+	bool seen_ready;
+	bool probing;
+	bool probe_sent;
+	bool pr_due;
+	bool pr_queued;
+	bool pr_sent;
+	bool sent_pr;
+	bool partner_drp;
+	unsigned int interval_ms;
+	unsigned long due;
+	ktime_t busy_since;
+	ktime_t sent_at;
+	ktime_t sink_at;
+	bool sink_by_swap;
+};
+
 struct tcpm_port {
 	struct device *dev;
 
@@ -625,6 +719,9 @@ struct tcpm_port {
 	/* Deadline in jiffies of tcpc->try_snk_extra_wait_ms, set in SNK_TRY */
 	unsigned long try_snk_wait_until;
 
+	/* tcpc->request_sink_as_source */
+	struct swap_back_data swap_back;
+
 	/* port belongs to a self powered device */
 	bool self_powered;
 
@@ -1847,6 +1944,677 @@ static int tcpm_request_dfp_as_sink(stru
 }
 
 /*
+ * Opt-in (tcpc->request_sink_as_source): the swap back to sink.
+ *
+ * A charge-through dock whose own supply goes away falls back to an
+ * unpowered sink; a port that prefers the sink role finds no source in
+ * Try.SNK and powers the dock.  When the dock's supply comes back, nothing on
+ * the link need say so, and the dock can stay on the port's power until it
+ * is re-plugged.
+ *
+ * So, as Source to a PD partner under an explicit contract, while the port
+ * prefers the sink role, the port asks the partner for its source
+ * capabilities (Get_Source_Cap, in GET_SOURCE_CAP) and requests a PR_Swap to
+ * Sink when their vSafe5V PDO says Unconstrained Power.  Nothing else ever
+ * leads to a PR_Swap.  The swap is TCPM's own PR_Swap; its failure paths are
+ * unchanged.
+ *
+ * The answers:
+ * - Unconstrained Power: PR_Swap.  Accepted, the port is to be sink at the
+ *   next ready state, in place or after the reconnect of an error recovery;
+ *   when the port is source there instead, the partner took the swap but
+ *   could not deliver, and the session stops.  Reject from a partner that
+ *   does not claim dual-role power, or Not_Supported: stop.  Any other
+ *   Reject, Wait or no answer: asked again later.
+ * - No Unconstrained Power: asked again after 30 s, then 60, 120, 240 and
+ *   480 s, then every 10 minutes; the partner's supply can come back at any
+ *   time.
+ * - Reject or Not_Supported (a sink now, as a charge-through dock may be while
+ *   its supply is away), or no answer: asked again every 10 minutes.
+ * The Dual-Role Power bit alone does not decide: a charge-through hub can
+ * pass on its charger's flags without it and still accept a PR_Swap.
+ *
+ * A session is one partner, across the reconnects that a failed swap causes
+ * itself: it ends once the port has been without a partner for
+ * SWAP_BACK_SESSION_GAP_MS.  A question or a request that was on the wire
+ * when a reset came stops the session: a partner that leaves the bus on
+ * either gets it once per session.  Per session, at most
+ * SWAP_BACK_MAX_REQUESTS requests and SWAP_BACK_MAX_ACCEPTED accepted swaps;
+ * a swap whose sink role lasted SWAP_BACK_SINK_REFUND_MS gives both back.  A
+ * swap that fails, or whose sink role is lost within SWAP_BACK_SINK_SHORT_MS
+ * with the port source again in the same session, is a strike and stops the
+ * session; so is a swap or a question that a reset cut short when the
+ * partner then stays away longer than the session's gap.  At
+ * SWAP_BACK_MAX_STRIKES nothing is asked in any session until a sink stint
+ * of SWAP_BACK_SINK_STABLE_MS has ended.
+ *
+ * Others' choices stand: a write of "source" to power_role, or a PR_Swap the
+ * partner asks for that makes the port source, stops the session.
+ *
+ * The work starts nothing while the VDM state machine runs, discovery is
+ * due, an AMS is open or a state change is queued, and GET_SOURCE_CAP sends
+ * nothing unless the AMS is still the question's.  The work runs on a
+ * freezable workqueue from a deferrable timer: it never wakes an idle CPU,
+ * and it does nothing while the system sleeps.
+ */
+
+/* One line in the TCPM log and the same one in the kernel log, formatted once */
+__printf(2, 3)
+static void tcpm_swap_back_info(struct tcpm_port *port, const char *fmt, ...)
+{
+	char buf[128];
+	va_list args;
+
+	va_start(args, fmt);
+	vsnprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), fmt, args);
+	va_end(args);
+	tcpm_log(port, "Swap back: %s", buf);
+	dev_info(port->dev, "swap back to sink: %s\n", buf);
+}
+
+/* Stop for the rest of the session; true when it had not stopped before */
+static bool tcpm_swap_back_halt(struct tcpm_port *port)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+
+	if (!port->tcpc->request_sink_as_source)
+		return false;
+	sb->pr_due = false;
+	cancel_delayed_work(&sb->work);
+	if (sb->stopped)
+		return false;
+	sb->stopped = true;
+	return true;
+}
+
+/* Stop for the rest of the session, saying why, once */
+__printf(2, 3)
+static void tcpm_swap_back_stop(struct tcpm_port *port, const char *fmt, ...)
+{
+	char buf[128];
+	va_list args;
+
+	if (!tcpm_swap_back_halt(port))
+		return;
+	va_start(args, fmt);
+	vsnprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), fmt, args);
+	va_end(args);
+	tcpm_log(port, "Swap back: stop: %s", buf);
+	dev_info(port->dev,
+		 "swap back to sink: %s; not asking again until the partner has been away for a minute\n",
+		 buf);
+}
+
+static bool tcpm_swap_back_wanted(struct tcpm_port *port)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+
+	return port->tcpc->request_sink_as_source && port->registered &&
+	       port->attached && port->pwr_role == TYPEC_SOURCE &&
+	       port->port_type == TYPEC_PORT_DRP &&
+	       port->try_role == TYPEC_SINK &&
+	       port->pd_capable && port->explicit_contract &&
+	       sb->armed && !sb->stopped &&
+	       sb->strikes < SWAP_BACK_MAX_STRIKES;
+}
+
+static void tcpm_swap_back_schedule(struct tcpm_port *port, unsigned int ms)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+
+	sb->due = jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(ms);
+	if (port->registered)
+		mod_delayed_work(system_freezable_power_efficient_wq, &sb->work,
+				 msecs_to_jiffies(ms));
+}
+
+/* Queue the work again at its due time if it should run and is not queued */
+static void tcpm_swap_back_kick(struct tcpm_port *port)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+
+	if (!tcpm_swap_back_wanted(port) || delayed_work_pending(&sb->work))
+		return;
+	mod_delayed_work(system_freezable_power_efficient_wq, &sb->work,
+			 time_after(sb->due, jiffies) ? sb->due - jiffies : 0);
+}
+
+/*
+ * After an answer that is not "yes": schedule the next question one step
+ * further down the ladder.  Returns the wait in seconds, for the log.
+ */
+static unsigned int tcpm_swap_back_backoff(struct tcpm_port *port)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+	unsigned int ms = sb->interval_ms;
+
+	sb->interval_ms = min(2 * ms, SWAP_BACK_POLL_MAX_MS);
+	tcpm_swap_back_schedule(port, ms);
+	return ms / 1000;
+}
+
+/*
+ * The port is busy, or a question was not sent: again in a second, for
+ * SWAP_BACK_BUSY_MAX_MS; after that, one step down the ladder.
+ */
+static void tcpm_swap_back_retry(struct tcpm_port *port)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+	ktime_t now = ktime_get_boottime();
+	unsigned int s;
+
+	if (!sb->busy_since)
+		sb->busy_since = now;
+	if (ktime_ms_delta(now, sb->busy_since) < SWAP_BACK_BUSY_MAX_MS) {
+		tcpm_swap_back_schedule(port, SWAP_BACK_RETRY_MS);
+		return;
+	}
+	sb->busy_since = 0;
+	s = tcpm_swap_back_backoff(port);
+	tcpm_log(port, "Swap back: port busy for a minute, asking again in %u s", s);
+}
+
+/* A question or a request goes on the wire now */
+static void tcpm_swap_back_sent(struct tcpm_port *port, bool pr_swap)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+
+	sb->sent_at = ktime_get_boottime();
+	sb->sent_pr = pr_swap;
+	sb->busy_since = 0;
+}
+
+/* Ask for the partner's source capabilities (GET_SOURCE_CAP) */
+static void tcpm_swap_back_probe(struct tcpm_port *port)
+{
+	port->upcoming_state = GET_SOURCE_CAP;
+	if (tcpm_ams_start(port, GET_SOURCE_CAPABILITIES) == -EAGAIN) {
+		port->upcoming_state = INVALID_STATE;
+		tcpm_swap_back_retry(port);
+		return;
+	}
+	port->swap_back.probing = true;
+}
+
+/* Request the sink role, as tcpm_pr_set() does, with nobody waiting */
+static void tcpm_swap_back_request(struct tcpm_port *port)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+
+	sb->pr_due = false;
+	if (sb->requests >= SWAP_BACK_MAX_REQUESTS) {
+		tcpm_swap_back_stop(port, "%u PR_Swap requests made",
+				    sb->requests);
+		return;
+	}
+	if (sb->accepted >= SWAP_BACK_MAX_ACCEPTED) {
+		tcpm_swap_back_stop(port, "%u swaps accepted", sb->accepted);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	port->upcoming_state = PR_SWAP_SEND;
+	if (tcpm_ams_start(port, POWER_ROLE_SWAP) == -EAGAIN) {
+		port->upcoming_state = INVALID_STATE;
+		sb->pr_due = true;
+		tcpm_swap_back_retry(port);
+		return;
+	}
+	sb->requests++;
+	sb->pr_queued = true;
+	tcpm_swap_back_info(port,
+			    "partner has external power (vSafe5V PDO %#010x), requesting the sink role, PR_Swap %u of %u",
+			    port->source_caps[0], sb->requests,
+			    SWAP_BACK_MAX_REQUESTS);
+}
+
+static void tcpm_swap_back_work(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	struct tcpm_port *port = container_of(to_delayed_work(work),
+					      struct tcpm_port, swap_back.work);
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+
+	mutex_lock(&port->lock);
+	if (!tcpm_swap_back_wanted(port))
+		goto unlock;
+
+	/* A run that waited for the lock while the schedule changed */
+	if (time_before(jiffies, sb->due)) {
+		mod_delayed_work(system_freezable_power_efficient_wq, &sb->work,
+				 sb->due - jiffies);
+		goto unlock;
+	}
+
+	/* Away from SRC_READY: tcpm_swap_back_ready() schedules again there */
+	if (port->state != SRC_READY)
+		goto unlock;
+
+	if (port->vdm_sm_running || port->send_discover ||
+	    port->send_discover_prime || port->ams != NONE_AMS ||
+	    port->upcoming_state != INVALID_STATE ||
+	    port->delayed_state != INVALID_STATE) {
+		tcpm_swap_back_retry(port);
+		goto unlock;
+	}
+
+	if (sb->pr_due)
+		tcpm_swap_back_request(port);
+	else
+		tcpm_swap_back_probe(port);
+
+unlock:
+	mutex_unlock(&port->lock);
+}
+
+/*
+ * A sink stint ends: at a port reset, or with the port source again without
+ * one (a swap the partner or the user asked for).  One that lasted
+ * SWAP_BACK_SINK_STABLE_MS clears the strikes and the session's counts, and
+ * at a reset the stop as well; one that came from a swap of the swap back's
+ * gives the budget back after SWAP_BACK_SINK_REFUND_MS, and is judged at the
+ * next ready state when it lasted less than SWAP_BACK_SINK_SHORT_MS.
+ */
+static void tcpm_swap_back_sink_ended(struct tcpm_port *port, ktime_t now,
+				      bool by_reset)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+	s64 ms = ktime_ms_delta(now, sb->sink_at);
+
+	if (ms >= SWAP_BACK_SINK_STABLE_MS) {
+		sb->strikes = 0;
+		sb->requests = 0;
+		sb->accepted = 0;
+		if (by_reset) {
+			sb->stopped = false;
+			sb->told_no_power = false;
+			sb->told_refused = false;
+		}
+	} else if (sb->sink_by_swap && ms >= SWAP_BACK_SINK_REFUND_MS) {
+		sb->requests = 0;
+		sb->accepted = 0;
+	} else if (sb->sink_by_swap && ms < SWAP_BACK_SINK_SHORT_MS) {
+		sb->lost_early = true;
+	}
+	sb->sink_at = 0;
+	sb->sink_by_swap = false;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Where SRC_READY and SNK_READY settle: a session starts at the first ready
+ * state after a gap, the outcome of an accepted swap and of a question is
+ * read, and the questions stay scheduled while the port is source.
+ */
+static void tcpm_swap_back_ready(struct tcpm_port *port)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+	ktime_t now;
+	unsigned int s;
+
+	if (!port->tcpc->request_sink_as_source)
+		return;
+
+	now = ktime_get_boottime();
+	if (!sb->seen_ready) {
+		sb->seen_ready = true;
+		/*
+		 * Without a partner for longer than a reconnect: a new one.  A
+		 * swap still pending, or a question or request that a reset
+		 * cut short, was the old partner's and counts as failed, but
+		 * stops nothing for the new one.  A sink role lost early was an
+		 * unplug.
+		 */
+		if (ktime_ms_delta(now, sb->reset_at) > SWAP_BACK_SESSION_GAP_MS) {
+			if (sb->pending || sb->unsettled) {
+				sb->strikes++;
+				tcpm_log(port,
+					 "Swap back: the last %s ended in a reset, failed swap %u of %u",
+					 sb->pending ? "swap" : "question",
+					 sb->strikes, SWAP_BACK_MAX_STRIKES);
+			}
+			sb->pending = false;
+			sb->lost_early = false;
+			sb->requests = 0;
+			sb->accepted = 0;
+			sb->stopped = false;
+			sb->told_no_power = false;
+			sb->told_refused = false;
+		}
+		/* The same partner again: the reset stopped the session already */
+		sb->unsettled = false;
+	}
+
+	if (port->pwr_role == TYPEC_SINK) {
+		/* Nothing of the swap back's is due while the port is sink */
+		sb->probing = false;
+		sb->probe_sent = false;
+		sb->pr_due = false;
+		sb->pr_queued = false;
+		sb->pr_sent = false;
+		sb->sent_at = 0;
+		if (!port->explicit_contract)
+			return;
+		sb->lost_early = false;
+		if (!sb->sink_at)
+			sb->sink_at = now;
+		if (sb->pending) {
+			sb->pending = false;
+			sb->sink_by_swap = true;
+			tcpm_swap_back_info(port, "power sink at %u mV %u mA%s",
+					    port->supply_voltage,
+					    port->current_limit,
+					    sb->pending_reset ?
+					    ", after a reconnect" : "");
+		}
+		return;
+	}
+
+	if (sb->sink_at)
+		tcpm_swap_back_sink_ended(port, now, false);
+	if (sb->lost_early) {
+		sb->lost_early = false;
+		sb->strikes++;
+		tcpm_swap_back_stop(port,
+				    "sink role lost within a minute of the swap, failed swap %u of %u",
+				    sb->strikes, SWAP_BACK_MAX_STRIKES);
+	}
+	if (sb->pending) {
+		/* Taken, but the partner did not become the source */
+		sb->pending = false;
+		sb->strikes++;
+		tcpm_swap_back_stop(port,
+				    "swap accepted but the partner did not supply power, failed swap %u of %u",
+				    sb->strikes, SWAP_BACK_MAX_STRIKES);
+	}
+	if (sb->probe_sent || sb->pr_sent) {
+		/* On the wire, and a Soft or Hard Reset came instead of an answer */
+		tcpm_swap_back_stop(port, "%s cut short",
+				    sb->pr_sent ? "PR_Swap" : "Get_Source_Cap");
+		sb->probe_sent = false;
+		sb->pr_sent = false;
+		sb->probing = false;
+		sb->pr_queued = false;
+		sb->sent_at = 0;
+	} else if (sb->probing) {
+		/* Never sent: a write or a message of the partner's came first */
+		sb->probing = false;
+		if (tcpm_swap_back_wanted(port))
+			tcpm_swap_back_retry(port);
+	} else if (sb->pr_queued) {
+		/* Never sent either: ask again later */
+		sb->pr_queued = false;
+		if (tcpm_swap_back_wanted(port)) {
+			s = tcpm_swap_back_backoff(port);
+			tcpm_swap_back_info(port,
+					    "PR_Swap request not sent, asking again in %u s",
+					    s);
+		}
+	}
+
+	if (!port->pd_capable || !port->explicit_contract)
+		return;
+
+	if (!sb->armed) {
+		sb->armed = true;
+		sb->interval_ms = SWAP_BACK_POLL_MIN_MS;
+		if (sb->strikes >= SWAP_BACK_MAX_STRIKES) {
+			tcpm_swap_back_stop(port,
+					    "paused after %u failed swaps until the port has been a power sink for %u minutes",
+					    sb->strikes,
+					    SWAP_BACK_SINK_STABLE_MS / 60000);
+			return;
+		}
+		sb->due = jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(SWAP_BACK_FIRST_MS);
+		if (tcpm_swap_back_wanted(port))
+			tcpm_swap_back_schedule(port, SWAP_BACK_FIRST_MS);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	if (sb->pr_due && tcpm_swap_back_wanted(port))
+		tcpm_swap_back_schedule(port, 0);
+	else
+		tcpm_swap_back_kick(port);
+}
+
+/*
+ * At every port reset.  The sink stint that it ends is judged
+ * (tcpm_swap_back_sink_ended()); an accepted swap that is still pending
+ * stays so, for the next ready state.  A question or a request that was on
+ * the wire, or sent less than SWAP_BACK_CUT_MS before and not answered, may
+ * be what made the partner leave: it stops the session, and it is a failed
+ * swap if the partner then stays away longer than the session's gap.
+ */
+static void tcpm_swap_back_reset(struct tcpm_port *port)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+	ktime_t now = ktime_get_boottime();
+
+	cancel_delayed_work(&sb->work);
+
+	if (sb->sink_at)
+		tcpm_swap_back_sink_ended(port, now, true);
+	if (sb->pending)
+		sb->pending_reset = true;
+	if (sb->probe_sent || sb->pr_sent ||
+	    (sb->sent_at &&
+	     ktime_ms_delta(now, sb->sent_at) < SWAP_BACK_CUT_MS)) {
+		tcpm_swap_back_stop(port, "%s cut short by a port reset",
+				    sb->pr_sent || (!sb->probe_sent && sb->sent_pr) ?
+				    "PR_Swap" : "Get_Source_Cap");
+		sb->unsettled = true;
+	}
+	/* A request that was about to go out is not for the next partner */
+	if ((sb->pr_queued && port->upcoming_state == PR_SWAP_SEND) ||
+	    (sb->probing && port->upcoming_state == GET_SOURCE_CAP))
+		port->upcoming_state = INVALID_STATE;
+
+	sb->reset_at = now;
+	sb->armed = false;
+	sb->seen_ready = false;
+	sb->probing = false;
+	sb->probe_sent = false;
+	sb->pr_due = false;
+	sb->pr_queued = false;
+	sb->pr_sent = false;
+	sb->partner_drp = false;
+	sb->interval_ms = SWAP_BACK_POLL_MIN_MS;
+	sb->busy_since = 0;
+	sb->sent_at = 0;
+	sb->sink_at = 0;
+	sb->sink_by_swap = false;
+}
+
+/* The partner's Source_Capabilities, in answer to GET_SOURCE_CAP */
+static void tcpm_swap_back_source_caps(struct tcpm_port *port)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+	unsigned int s;
+	u32 pdo;
+
+	sb->probing = false;
+	sb->probe_sent = false;
+	sb->sent_at = 0;
+	if (!tcpm_swap_back_wanted(port))
+		return;
+	if (!port->nr_source_caps ||
+	    pdo_type(port->source_caps[0]) != PDO_TYPE_FIXED) {
+		tcpm_swap_back_stop(port,
+				    "the partner's source capabilities do not start with a fixed supply");
+		return;
+	}
+
+	pdo = port->source_caps[0];
+	sb->partner_drp = pdo & PDO_FIXED_DUAL_ROLE;
+	if (pdo & PDO_FIXED_EXTPOWER) {
+		/* tcpm_swap_back_ready() starts the request from SRC_READY */
+		tcpm_log(port, "Swap back: partner has external power, dual-role power %s",
+			 str_yes_no(sb->partner_drp));
+		sb->pr_due = true;
+		return;
+	}
+
+	s = tcpm_swap_back_backoff(port);
+	if (sb->told_no_power) {
+		tcpm_log(port, "Swap back: no external power, asking again in %u s", s);
+		return;
+	}
+	sb->told_no_power = true;
+	tcpm_swap_back_info(port,
+			    "partner has no external power now, asking again in %u s, then less often down to every %u s",
+			    s, SWAP_BACK_POLL_MAX_MS / 1000);
+}
+
+/*
+ * Not a source now: Reject or Not_Supported to Get_Source_Cap, or no answer.
+ * A charge-through dock may well answer so while its supply is away, so ask
+ * again, at the slow end of the ladder; this never leads to a PR_Swap by
+ * itself.
+ */
+static void tcpm_swap_back_no_source(struct tcpm_port *port,
+				     const char *answer)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+	unsigned int s;
+
+	sb->probing = false;
+	sb->probe_sent = false;
+	if (!tcpm_swap_back_wanted(port))
+		return;
+	sb->interval_ms = SWAP_BACK_POLL_MAX_MS;
+	s = tcpm_swap_back_backoff(port);
+	if (sb->told_refused) {
+		tcpm_log(port, "Swap back: Get_Source_Cap answered %s, asking again in %u s",
+			 answer, s);
+		return;
+	}
+	sb->told_refused = true;
+	tcpm_swap_back_info(port,
+			    "Get_Source_Cap answered %s, not a source now, asking again every %u s",
+			    answer, s);
+}
+
+/* Reject, Wait or Not_Supported in answer to GET_SOURCE_CAP */
+static void tcpm_swap_back_probe_refused(struct tcpm_port *port,
+					 enum pd_ctrl_msg_type type)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+	unsigned int s;
+
+	sb->sent_at = 0;
+	if (type != PD_CTRL_WAIT) {
+		tcpm_swap_back_no_source(port, type == PD_CTRL_REJECT ?
+					 "Reject" : "Not_Supported");
+		return;
+	}
+	sb->probing = false;
+	sb->probe_sent = false;
+	if (!tcpm_swap_back_wanted(port))
+		return;
+	s = tcpm_swap_back_backoff(port);
+	tcpm_log(port, "Swap back: Get_Source_Cap answered Wait, asking again in %u s", s);
+}
+
+/*
+ * GET_SOURCE_CAP: no answer (0), or the transmit failed (< 0).  A message
+ * the TCPC discarded for an incoming one did not go out: the next ready
+ * state retries it.  Any other failure may have reached the partner and
+ * counts as sent, without an answer.
+ */
+static void tcpm_swap_back_probe_failed(struct tcpm_port *port, int ret)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+
+	if (ret == -EAGAIN) {
+		sb->sent_at = 0;
+		return;
+	}
+	if (ret)
+		tcpm_log(port, "Swap back: Get_Source_Cap not sent whole (%d)", ret);
+	tcpm_swap_back_no_source(port, "nothing");
+}
+
+/* PR_SWAP_SEND: tell whose request goes out */
+static void tcpm_swap_back_pr_send(struct tcpm_port *port)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+
+	sb->pr_sent = sb->pr_queued;
+	sb->pr_queued = false;
+	if (sb->pr_sent)
+		tcpm_swap_back_sent(port, true);
+}
+
+/*
+ * PR_SWAP_ACCEPT: the partner asked for a power role swap and gets it.  A
+ * request of the swap back's that was queued is dropped there (the partner's
+ * swap gives the role it asked for), a question that was queued goes too (it
+ * would go out in the other power role), and a partner that asks for the sink
+ * role itself, making the port source, is not asked to take it back.
+ */
+static void tcpm_swap_back_partner_swap(struct tcpm_port *port)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+
+	sb->pr_queued = false;
+	sb->pr_due = false;
+	if (sb->probing && port->upcoming_state == GET_SOURCE_CAP) {
+		port->upcoming_state = INVALID_STATE;
+		sb->probing = false;
+	}
+	if (port->pwr_role == TYPEC_SINK)
+		tcpm_swap_back_stop(port, "the partner asked for the sink role");
+}
+
+/*
+ * The partner's answer to a PR_Swap of the swap back's: Accept, Reject,
+ * Wait, Not_Supported, or 0 for none.
+ */
+static void tcpm_swap_back_pr_answer(struct tcpm_port *port,
+				     enum pd_ctrl_msg_type type)
+{
+	struct swap_back_data *sb = &port->swap_back;
+	const char *answer;
+	unsigned int s;
+
+	if (!sb->pr_sent)
+		return;
+	sb->pr_sent = false;
+	if (type)
+		sb->sent_at = 0;
+
+	switch (type) {
+	case PD_CTRL_ACCEPT:
+		sb->accepted++;
+		sb->pending = true;
+		sb->pending_reset = false;
+		tcpm_swap_back_info(port, "PR_Swap accepted, swap %u of %u",
+				    sb->accepted, SWAP_BACK_MAX_ACCEPTED);
+		return;
+	case PD_CTRL_NOT_SUPP:
+		tcpm_swap_back_stop(port, "PR_Swap answered Not_Supported");
+		return;
+	case PD_CTRL_REJECT:
+		if (!sb->partner_drp) {
+			tcpm_swap_back_stop(port,
+					    "PR_Swap answered Reject by a partner that does not claim dual-role power");
+			return;
+		}
+		answer = "Reject";
+		break;
+	case PD_CTRL_WAIT:
+		answer = "Wait";
+		break;
+	default:
+		answer = "nothing";
+		break;
+	}
+
+	if (!tcpm_swap_back_wanted(port))
+		return;
+	s = tcpm_swap_back_backoff(port);
+	tcpm_swap_back_info(port, "PR_Swap answered %s, asking again in %u s",
+			    answer, s);
+}
